From 14dc789be5eefd5a44eb13d3d8d711de8caeb30a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 20:08:59 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 626/638] aros: --aros-pin-workers places threads and child
 processes round-robin from CPU 1

AROS never migrates a task and a new task inherits only its creator's
CPU, so Chromium sized its pools from KrnGetCPUCount() and then ran every
thread on CPU 0. MaybePinThreadRoundRobin() gives each pthread an
affinity mask for the next core (starting at 1: CPU 0 already carries
the main thread, Intuition, input and the handlers); ArosAllocChildCpuMask()
does the same for CreateNewProc() via NP_Affinity, which exec takes
ownership of. Both print one "[Chromium:SMP]" line per placement on
serial so placement is grep-able rather than inferred.

The switch is re-checked until CommandLine is initialised, then latched:
threads are created before CommandLine::Init() in some processes and a
static-const-bool at the call site latched "off" for the process.

The AROS kernel headers stay in platform_thread_aros.cc: <aros/kernel.h>
defines an Allocate macro that collides with PartitionAlloc's
state_bitmap.h when pulled into platform_thread_posix.cc.

Note this only works with the sysroot libpthread (12856aa052); with the
stale hosted archive collect-aros used to link, pthread_attr_t had no
cpuaffinity field and this placed nothing.


---
 base/process/launch_aros.cc                   |  20 +-
 base/threading/platform_thread_aros.cc        | 191 ++++++++++++++++++
 .../platform_thread_internal_posix.h          |  34 ++++
 base/threading/platform_thread_posix.cc       |   9 +
 4 files changed, 252 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

